WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:04.750
TobiWan has been called the voice of Dota 2.

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:10.030
He’s one of the most well known and well
respected broadcast talents in professional

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:12.440
competitive gaming today.

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:14.800
He’s also one hell of a karaoke singer.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:21.920
(Karaoke)

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:22.940
Hello there.

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:27.320
I’m Colin from theScore esports, and today,
we’re taking a look, or rather a listen,

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:31.960
at the best of Toby Dawson, AKA TobiWan.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:36.580
Now I know you guys know TobiWan primarily
for Dota, but he actually got his start in

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:38.720
the Australian Call of Duty scene.

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:43.920
He’s also dabbled in CS:GO, and done PUBG
hosting and commentary as well.

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:47.980
Now before we get into those games guys, I
am going to give you what you came for, those

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.540
iconic Dota 2 TobiWan calls.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:07:18.580
(Casting)

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:22.880
Now, I can’t be the only guy who got goosebumps
from hearing those calls again, can I?

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:29.880
Those are the iconic, serious, TobiWan Dota
2 calls, but we’d be doing the man a disservice

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:34.300
if we didn’t acknowledge his more meme-y,
kooky, wacky side.

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:36.520
And that’s what this next section is all
about.

00:07:36.520 --> 00:08:15.360
(Karaoke)

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:20.480
(Casting)

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:47.040
Oh my god, it's a black hooooooooooooooooooooooooooole.

00:08:48.260 --> 00:09:38.500
(Casting)

00:09:41.840 --> 00:09:43.440
Hello.

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:45.840
My name's Toby.

00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:47.680
TobiWan.

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:55.360
Would you like a Dota?

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:02.960
I could eat 9000 of these.

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:04.780
Over 9000.

00:10:05.220 --> 00:10:08.900
My mama always said,  life is like a box of Dota.

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:11.540
You never know when you're going to get hooked.

00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:15.740
I realize I put you on the spot, but they did have an over 10 kill advantage

00:10:16.640 --> 00:10:18.660
Camera X, camera X.

00:10:20.020 --> 00:10:21.860
It's a disaster.

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:24.880
Thank you so much, I want to put that on my FaceBook page.

00:10:24.960 --> 00:11:44.320
(Casting)

00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:48.560
Now guys, this video would not be complete
if we didn’t acknowledge the other games

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:50.720
that TobiWan has left his mark on.

00:11:50.720 --> 00:11:54.480
He’s not just Dota 2 after all, as I said
in the intro, he’s done COD, he’s done

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:57.520
CS:GO, and he’s done PUBG as well.

00:11:57.520 --> 00:12:02.000
And in true TobiWan fashion, he’s left us
with some hilarious one-liners from each one

00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:03.200
of those.

00:12:03.200 --> 00:13:42.960
(Casting)

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:45.320
Alright guys, that’s all we got for you
this week.

00:13:45.320 --> 00:13:48.160
What was your favourite TobiWan call or moment?

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:50.160
And is there a player, a topic, or

00:13:50.160 --> 00:13:53.320
team you want to see us cover in a future video?

00:13:53.720 --> 00:13:57.720
If so, let me know in the comments below and
I will see you next week.

